203 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 74 0 R
/E (TfidfVectorizer transforms occupational descriptions into numerical feature vectors. Key parameters: max_features=8000 \(vocabulary size\), ngram_range=\(1,2\) for unigrams and bigrams, min_df=2 to filter rare terms. This creates a high-dimensional vector space where similar occupations cluster together.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
204 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 74 0 R
/E (Feature extraction captures semantic meaning from O*NET occupation descriptions. Each occupation becomes a sparse vector of 8,000 weighted term frequencies, enabling mathematical comparison of career profiles.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
205 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
